"; =====================================================================\r\n"
"; FF7 Remake co-op mod settings\r\n"
"; Edit with Notepad or the settings app, save, then press F6 in game (ReloadKey) - or restart the game:\r\n"
";   some settings only change at a restart (see ReloadKey below). Lines starting with ; are notes.\r\n"
"; Delete this file to get the defaults back (it is re-created on the next launch).\r\n"
";\r\n"
"; Controller button names: A B X Y LB RB LT RT L3 R3 Start Back\r\n"
";                          DPadUp DPadDown DPadLeft DPadRight None\r\n"
";   Several buttons for one action: separate with commas, e.g.  LB, LT\r\n"
"; Keyboard key names: Up Down Left Right Enter Escape Space Tab Backspace,\r\n"
";   single letters/digits (Z, X, 1), F1-F12, Num0-Num9\r\n"
"; Which controller each player uses: [Input2] at the end of this file (Auto = the mod picks).\r\n"
"; =====================================================================\r\n"
"\r\n"
"[General]\r\n"
"; Mod hotkeys only work in normal play (walking around or fighting), never in menus, pause\r\n"
";   screens or cutscenes - the game uses F1-F8 in its menus. Keep them off Ctrl/Alt/Shift:\r\n"
";   those guard, dash and open shortcuts in this game. None = no key.\r\n"
"; Key that makes player 2 join or leave\r\n"
"JoinKey=F10\r\n"
"; Hot swap keys: the person who started as player 1 / 2 / 3 takes the lead (the party\r\n"
";   leader, main menu, chests) and trades characters with whoever leads right now. Each\r\n"
";   person keeps their own controller. Keyboard only (player 1's decision). The keyboard\r\n"
";   always drives the leader, so player 1 should be on a controller to play a teammate.\r\n"
"LeadKeyPlayer1=F9\r\n"
"LeadKeyPlayer2=Ctrl+F9\r\n"
"LeadKeyPlayer3=Shift+F9\r\n"
"; Key that re-reads this file while the game runs (change settings without restarting).\r\n"
";   These need a restart: [Input2] SeatN (which controller / player 3 on or off),\r\n"
";   JoinAtStart and the split screen's Enabled / Show.\r\n"
"ReloadKey=F6\r\n"
"; Key that shows / hides a list of all the co-op keys and controller buttons on screen\r\n"
"HelpKey=F5\r\n"
"; 1 = show the frame rate at the top of the screen\r\n"
"ShowFPS=0\r\n"
"; 1 = show the PC's clock (the same time as the log lines) in the top right corner - for noting times while testing\r\n"
"ShowClock=0\r\n"
"; Own command menus: 1 = after players 2/3 give a command in their own menu it closes (the game would turn it to player 1's page and leave it open), 0 = off\r\n"
"OwnMenuCloseAfterCommand=1\r\n"
"; 1 = while the leader plays on the keyboard, the hot swap keys do nothing (the keyboard only works for the\r\n"
";   leader, so a swap would leave that player watching the AI - default); 0 = hot swap always works\r\n"
"KeyboardLeaderKeepsLead=1\r\n"

"; Auto = player 2 starts joined if their controller is connected (or joins as soon as it connects); 0 = press\r\n"
";   JoinKey / hold JoinButton first\r\n"
"JoinAtStart=Auto\r\n"
"; 1 = show players 2/3's target markers (P2 green, P3 orange)\r\n"
"ShowTargetMarker=1\r\n"
"; 1 = show the P2/P3 badges in the top-right corner (diamonds: \"PLAYER\" in the player's color = a person\r\n"
";   is playing that character, red \"AI\" = the game's AI is, faded gray = no character in that slot)\r\n"
"ShowStatusCircles=1\r\n"
"; Where they sit: distance in from the right edge and down from the top (pixels at 1080p),\r\n"
";   and a size multiplier. Raise StatusCirclesTop if they cover the minimap.\r\n"
"StatusCirclesRight=12\r\n"
"StatusCirclesTop=12\r\n"
"StatusCirclesSize=0.5\r\n"
"; 1 = when player 2 is off screen, show a circle at the screen edge in their direction.\r\n"
";   The arrow inside it is the way player 2 is facing (pointing back toward the middle of the\r\n"
";   screen = coming back into view, pointing outward = heading further away).\r\n"
"ShowOffscreenArrow=1\r\n"

"; 1 = while player 2 or 3 is in, the AI teammates guard when player 1 guards (like the normal\r\n"
";   game does on its own). 0 = off.\r\n"
"AIGuardCopy=1\r\n"
"\r\n"
"[Camera]\r\n"
"; Shared co-op camera. It keeps both players and their current targets in view, adds other\r\n"
"; nearby enemies when that's cheap, zooms out as needed and tilts down toward an overhead view\r\n"
"; as everything spreads out. Player 1 still turns the camera. Distances: game units (~1 cm).\r\n"
"Enabled=1\r\n"
"; Key to switch the co-op camera on/off while playing (to compare with the normal camera)\r\n"
"ToggleKey=F8\r\n"
"; (While the split-screen windows (F7) show, each player has their own view and the co-op camera is off.)\r\n"
"; Side-by-side split screen: 1 = while player 1 is locked on, the game's lock-on view is centred in player 1's half (0 = player 1 always in the middle of their half)\r\n"
"SplitAimFollowsLockOn=1\r\n"
"; With SplitAimFollowsLockOn: 1 = turn toward the locked-on enemy only as far as player 1 stays in their part of the\r\n"
";   screen (the enemy may sit off centre), 0 = the enemy always in the middle (player 1 can leave the view)\r\n"
"SplitAimLockKeepsPlayer1=1\r\n"
"; With SplitAimFollowsLockOn: 1 = player 1's view widens (up to +60%, at most 110 degrees) when needed so the locked-on\r\n"
";   enemy can stay centred with player 1 still in view; 0 = never changes player 1's field of view\r\n"
"SplitAimLockZoom=1\r\n"
"; Side-by-side split: 1 = player 1's view is moved into their part with an off-centre lens (no squeeze at\r\n"
";   the screen edge, best for thirds); 0 = the camera is turned instead (the old way)\r\n"
"SplitLens=1\r\n"
"; Where the camera aims: 0.0 = on player 1, 1.0 = the middle of everything being framed\r\n"
"Bias=0.4\r\n"
"; The closest the camera gets to player 1 (cm; 800 = 8 m)\r\n"
"BaseZoomOut=800\r\n"
"; Farthest the camera may pull back\r\n"
"MaxDistance=3500\r\n"
"; How much of the screen the framed characters may use (0.8 = keep a border around them)\r\n"
"ScreenMargin=0.6\r\n"
"; Steepest downward angle when everything is spread out (degrees; 90 = straight down)\r\n"
"MaxTilt=35\r\n"
"; The camera starts tilting down when things are this spread out...\r\n"
"TiltStartSpread=800\r\n"
"; ...and reaches MaxTilt at this spread\r\n"
"TiltFullSpread=3000\r\n"
"; Other enemies (not anyone's current target) within this distance of player 1 are framed too...\r\n"
"EnemyRadius=2500\r\n"
"; ...but only if that pulls the camera back by no more than this fraction (0.25 = 25% more)\r\n"
"EnemyExtraAllowance=0.25\r\n"
"; How quickly the camera eases into its new position (higher = snappier, lower = floatier)\r\n"
"Smoothing=3.0\r\n"
"; If the game's own camera is further than this from player 1, it's a scripted shot or\r\n"
";   cutscene: the co-op camera stays out of it (it also stays out of real cutscenes)\r\n"
"CutsceneDistance=3000\r\n"
"; 1 = during talking scenes and cinematic shots (the game takes away the field controls, or narrows its camera) the co-op camera\r\n"
";   and the split screen step aside for the game's own camera, 0 = they stay on\r\n"
"TalkScenes=1\r\n"
"; 1 = move the camera in front of walls/ceilings that would block the view (characters, enemies and props are ignored), 0 = off\r\n"
"WallCheck=1\r\n"
"; If even MaxDistance can't fit everyone, slowly turn the camera to look from behind player 1\r\n"
";   toward player 2, and turn back when they come together. Grabbing the camera cancels it.\r\n"
"AutoOrient=1\r\n"
"; How fast it turns, in degrees per second\r\n"
"AutoOrientSpeed=60\r\n"
"\r\n"
"[PictureInPicture]\r\n"
"; A small second view that follows player 2 (picture-in-picture). It draws the game a second\r\n"
