"\r\n"
"[Input2]\r\n"
"; Which controller each player uses: Keyboard, None, Auto, or a controller's model number\r\n"
";   VID:PID as the settings app shows it (e.g. 054C:0CE6 = DualSense, 0D22:0C34 = msi GC30).\r\n"
";   Two controllers of the same model: 045E:028E#1 and 045E:028E#2.\r\n"
"; Auto = the first free gamepad (never a wheel, pedals or a flight stick). Seats are filled in\r\n"
";   order, so with one controller player 1 gets it. A player keeps their controller when it is\r\n"
";   unplugged and plugged in again.\r\n"
"; Player 1 always has the keyboard as well; Seat1=Keyboard = player 1 on the keyboard only.\r\n"
"; Seat3=None switches player 3 off.\r\n"
"Seat1=Auto\r\n"
"Seat2=Auto\r\n"
"Seat3=Auto\r\n"
"; XInput = the game only ever sees the party leader's controller (leave it like this)\r\n"
"GameInput=XInput\r\n"
"\r\n"
"; A controller whose buttons come out wrong (some generic controllers): its own button map, by\r\n"
";   model number - the settings app writes it when you set the buttons. By hand, e.g.:\r\n"
"; [Pad.0D22:0C34]\r\n"
"; Name=msi GC30 V2\r\n"
"; A=1\r\n"
"; B=2\r\n"
";   ... X Y LB RB LT RT Back Start LS RS = the button numbers Windows shows (1 = first),\r\n"
";   LeftX LeftY RightX RightY = X Y Z Rx Ry Rz Slider1 Slider2 (the stick axes)\r\n"
;
